Jaguar unveiled its first-ever SUV in  May and since then things have been  looking up for the formerly stuffy  British brand the company says the SUV  accounted for half of its US sales in  July so what's got people flocking to  this new cat I found a lot to discover  when I took the S case for a spin around  New York City I drove the F pace our  sport which starts at $54,000 but will  run you close to 64,000 with upgrades it  has a 340 horsepower supercharged v6  engine it's no Porsche Cayenne Turbo S  but it will get you to 60 miles per hour  in five four seconds top speed is 155  miles per hour  the steering standard all-wheel drive  and 8-speed automatic transmission ours  like a young jumping cat the exterior of  the car is exciting to choose the  metallic British racing green that my  car had it costs an extra few hundred  dollars but with the extremely fair  pricing on this thing you can afford it  jag has kept the wide rounded lattice  grill and the flashy red Jaguar logos it  also has stretched the body of the rig  long enough so that it looks lean and  mean ready to pounce this is no beefy  beer-drinking grit  it's a spelt jungle feline inside the  best part is the massive panoramic  sunroof big sunroof expands basically  the entire ceiling of the car it adds a  lot of natural light it makes it some  really big without increasing the  wheelbase at all  I congratulate jack for giving us  well-made leather top seats intuitive  controls and even ambient mood lighting  the touchscreen is nice and long and it  works well I'd love to see a better  resolution bill on the exterior cameras  and then there are the doors the lofts  and the window controls they're on two  different levels the bottom line jaguar  has a hit at least a triple with the F  pace it's stylish athletic and eager on  the road have you driven a Jaguar lately  if you haven't make it this one
 

